{"campaign_id": "rq2_multimodel_held_out", "citations": [], "contradiction_status": [], "escalated": true, "evidence_gaps": ["At least one retrieved technical artifact supporting the incident judgment."], "evidence_requests": 1, "final_report": {"claim_support": [{"cited_artifact_id": "", "claim": "Serious potential patient-safety risk due to missed arrhythmia detection leading to stroke", "support_note": "Cited ID was not retrieved or is a hallucination trap.", "support_status": "unsupported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "mdr-art83-pms-system", "claim": "EU MDR Article 83(1)-(2) requires post-market surveillance analysis", "support_note": "Regulatory text explicitly mandates gathering and analyzing data on device safety throughout its lifetime.", "support_status": "supported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "", "claim": "No causal link established between retrieved artifacts and the incident", "support_note": "Cited ID was not retrieved or is a hallucination trap.", "support_status": "unsupported"}], "confidence": 0.45, "evidence_links": [], "missing_evidence": ["At least one retrieved technical artifact supporting the incident judgment."], "rationale": "The incident narrative reports a confirmed embolic stroke temporally linked to an unflagged rapid-ventricular-response atrial fibrillation episode (likely ventricular tachycardia). This represents a serious potential patient-safety risk involving the failure of a safety-critical function (arrhythmia detection), which could have led to serious harm. However, no technical artifact retrieved explicitly describes this specific event or confirms that an unflagged rapid-ventricular-response episode occurred in production; all provided artifacts are synthetic logs for unrelated firmware modules or pre-dating versions without causal linkage to the incident. The only code diff is from a different version and predates the device state relevant to the report, failing to establish causality between any change and the event. Consequently, while the clinical outcome warrants immediate investigation under EU MDR Article 83(1)-(2) for post-market surveillance analysis of quality, performance, and safety data (mdr-art83-pms-system), there is insufficient evidence to confirm recurrence or a specific technical root cause requiring field safety corrective action at this stage. The low confidence stems from the absence of direct correlation between any retrieved artifact and the reported clinical failure.", "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "requires_human_review": true, "severity": 3}, "final_report_sha256": "096392d36bf577448d951eafc9dda7a5fa435e2c4de999f02bcef1e0014f497b", "generation_source": "ollama_real", "invalid_proposals": 1, "is_fallback": false, "is_mock": false, "opa_actions": ["technical_incident_missing_technical_evidence", "deny:technical_incident_missing_technical_evidence"], "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "record_type": "terminal", "report_id": "SYN-IND-0034", "retrievals": 1, "revisions": 1, "run_id": "SYN-IND-0034_r2", "scenario_id": "SYN-IND-0034", "schema_version": "2.1.0", "severity": 3, "shacl_findings": [], "state_terminal": "terminal", "termination_reason": "human escalation or invalid transition", "timestamp_utc": "2026-08-04T19:01:20.992954Z", "total_steps": 6, "trace_id": "0256a929-2845-4c08-9d73-aa4525579383"}
